WEBVTT

01:34.635 --> 01:38.847
DELICIOUS IN DUNGEON

01:51.193 --> 01:53.028
I slept too long!

01:59.451 --> 02:01.745
I don't hear anything.

02:01.829 --> 02:02.955
There's no heartbeat.

02:03.622 --> 02:05.749
It's because you're listening
through his armor.

02:07.042 --> 02:09.336
Looks like
he finally managed to fall asleep.

02:10.796 --> 02:13.966
I suppose that means
his food poisoning settled down.

02:14.716 --> 02:17.469
Oh, Laios. What a troublemaker.

02:17.553 --> 02:19.513
Let's let him sleep a bit longer.

02:19.596 --> 02:21.974
He was tossing and turning
all through the night.

02:22.891 --> 02:25.144
I wonder about this dungeon,

02:25.227 --> 02:28.981
does it already know how many monsters
need to be defeated on each floor?

02:29.815 --> 02:33.402
Killing monsters in here
just stabilizes the ecosystem.

02:33.485 --> 02:35.112
But if we don't do it,

02:35.195 --> 02:37.239
the village will get
completely overrun by them.

02:38.031 --> 02:41.702
And when the village does get overwhelmed,
it recruits adventurers to help.

02:42.452 --> 02:44.997
Hmm. Pretty clever system.

02:45.080 --> 02:47.040
What are you talking about?

02:47.124 --> 02:49.751
About how dungeons are made,
isn't it obvious?

02:50.335 --> 02:51.712
It was a while ago,

02:51.795 --> 02:53.839
but I studied it
back when I was in school.

02:54.506 --> 02:56.633
It's a lot more complex than you'd think.

02:58.343 --> 03:00.721
Hey, isn't that Marcille?

03:00.804 --> 03:03.015
You know, from the graduate course.

03:03.098 --> 03:05.601
She was the school's very first genius!

03:05.684 --> 03:09.646
Yeah. I heard she was
the teacher's assistant the first day.

03:09.730 --> 03:11.398
And I heard that
they've decided

03:11.481 --> 03:13.108
she's going to be a court magician.

03:13.192 --> 03:14.860
Really? That's amazing!

03:16.486 --> 03:19.907
Actually, I wasn't assisting the teacher
until the fifth day of school,

03:19.990 --> 03:23.160
and the court magician thing,
it's 'cause my mom was one too.

03:25.537 --> 03:29.291
By the way, I kind of pestered the teacher
to let me join class today.

03:30.000 --> 03:31.877
So, hi. Glad to be here.

03:32.961 --> 03:35.047
Uh, hey.

03:36.089 --> 03:39.551
Today, we're going to experiment
with spirit cultivation.

03:40.135 --> 03:43.013
I want each of you to grab a jar
and head outside.

03:44.848 --> 03:47.184
<i>Using wooden disks</i>
<i>with a hole in them,</i>

03:47.267 --> 03:50.646
<i>place the disk,</i>
<i>and then a layer of soil on top,</i>

03:50.729 --> 03:52.064
<i>and begin alternating.</i>

03:53.398 --> 03:55.150
<i>Create a barrier over it,</i>

03:55.651 --> 03:58.403
<i>and then, fill the jar with mana,</i>

03:59.279 --> 04:01.281
<i>release some spirits inside.</i>

04:03.784 --> 04:06.995
<i>The microscopic spirits will live off</i>
<i>the mana in the vessel.</i>

04:07.788 --> 04:11.208
<i>They'll die if the mana</i>
<i>is too dense or too thin.</i>

04:11.291 --> 04:14.920
<i>Raising spirits is the foundation</i>
<i>for summoning magic.</i>

04:15.003 --> 04:17.214
<i>The vessel we keep them in</i>
<i>is called a "dungeonium",</i>

04:17.297 --> 04:20.550
<i>because it looks similar to the structure</i>
<i>of a monster-ridden dungeon.</i>

04:21.885 --> 04:24.346
When you're finished,
place it in the darkroom.

04:24.429 --> 04:26.932
We'll see how they're doing
in a week's time.

04:28.225 --> 04:31.812
Wow, Marcille,
your barrier is so pretty!

04:31.895 --> 04:33.981
I can't believe
this was your first time.

04:34.064 --> 04:36.984
Although, why the interest
in summoning magic?

04:37.067 --> 04:39.987
-Huh?
-It's not like it's your specialty.

04:40.570 --> 04:43.699
I've been researching things
to learn how to build a safe dungeon.

04:44.408 --> 04:46.368
I'm on magic ingredients now.

04:47.202 --> 04:48.495
For example,

04:48.578 --> 04:52.040
<i>ingredients like Mandrakes</i>
<i>are pretty dangerous to harvest.</i>

04:53.083 --> 04:56.295
However, if we could create a safe dungeon

04:56.378 --> 04:58.755
that's inhabited
by monsters that are useful,

04:58.839 --> 05:01.383
then it would greatly contribute
to society.

05:01.466 --> 05:03.427
Uh, wow.

05:03.510 --> 05:05.012
That sounds amazing.

05:05.095 --> 05:06.722
Look at Marcille's barrier!

05:06.805 --> 05:08.348
It's so enchanting!

05:08.432 --> 05:09.725
Hey, can I see too?

05:09.808 --> 05:11.518
Make some room for me!

05:11.601 --> 05:13.562
-Careful!
-Huh?

05:15.981 --> 05:17.149
Are you hurt?

05:17.232 --> 05:19.026
Oh. No, I'm okay.

05:22.738 --> 05:25.282
<i>There are some impurities</i>
<i>mixed in the soil,</i>

05:25.365 --> 05:28.660
<i>and the mana's thin</i>
<i>'cause the barrier is full of holes.</i>

05:29.411 --> 05:32.622
<i>In that state,</i>
<i>the spirits inside won't live long.</i>

05:32.706 --> 05:34.875
You didn't get dirt
on your clothes, did you?

05:34.958 --> 05:35.792
Huh?

05:35.876 --> 05:38.378
That girl, she's always covered in dirt

05:38.462 --> 05:41.214
and ditches class,
so people think she's weird.

05:42.549 --> 05:43.508
Huh.

05:46.720 --> 05:49.973
Now then, when everyone
has their jars in front of them,

05:50.057 --> 05:53.435
we'll see how your spirits have developed
over the past week.

05:53.518 --> 05:56.229
Are you kidding?
Mine are all dead!

05:56.313 --> 05:58.065
Wow, mine somehow survived!

05:58.148 --> 05:59.733
Is this a new type of spirit?

05:59.816 --> 06:00.942
You mean the mold?

06:01.985 --> 06:04.196
<i>If a good number of them survived,</i>

06:04.279 --> 06:05.947
<i>the fire will be large.</i>

06:08.450 --> 06:11.203
It looks like your spirits
are being maintained nicely.

06:11.286 --> 06:13.038
Excellent work, Marcille.

06:18.210 --> 06:19.211
Uh-oh.

06:19.920 --> 06:22.339
Uh, what's happening to my jar?

06:22.923 --> 06:25.092
That's quite a lot of spirits there.

06:25.175 --> 06:26.468
What do I do?

06:27.052 --> 06:29.596
Don't worry, I'll handle it.

06:29.679 --> 06:32.849
Please tell me, how did you do that?
I need to know!

06:32.933 --> 06:35.352
Uh, well, you see, I…

06:35.435 --> 06:38.563
I know a place pretty close by
that has a lot of spirits,

06:38.647 --> 06:41.858
I thought my dungeonium would work better
if I used soil from there.

06:41.942 --> 06:44.361
Huh? There's a place like that nearby?

06:44.444 --> 06:45.612
Can you tell me where?

06:46.196 --> 06:47.989
Uh, it's, uh…

06:48.073 --> 06:50.700
This is the same amount
as in a real dungeon.

06:50.784 --> 06:53.203
This will be a fine sample indeed.

06:56.957 --> 06:59.126
I got it from a real dungeon.

07:02.337 --> 07:04.089
We can get outside from here.

07:05.632 --> 07:08.510
This was here the whole time?

07:22.649 --> 07:23.775
Huh?

07:30.365 --> 07:33.201
So, are you always doing stuff like this?

07:33.285 --> 07:34.286
Yup!

07:36.997 --> 07:39.040
That's why people think she's weird.

07:48.717 --> 07:50.510
It's a bug!

07:50.594 --> 07:52.387
Delicious fruits!

07:54.473 --> 07:57.142
You can't just pick up
and eat random crap you find!

07:57.225 --> 08:00.145
You've got to be careful!
What if those things poisoned you?

08:00.228 --> 08:03.148
Oh, but I actually know
what these things are.

08:03.732 --> 08:06.151
Grasshoppers and raspberries
aren't poisonous.

08:12.032 --> 08:14.159
So it really is a dungeon.

08:14.242 --> 08:15.869
This is amazing.

08:18.163 --> 08:21.249
<i>The mana here is stagnant,</i>
<i>and the air is stale.</i>

08:21.333 --> 08:23.585
<i>It seems like it's a natural cave.</i>

08:24.377 --> 08:26.546
Wait, don't go in there!

08:27.964 --> 08:29.049
Huh?

08:32.260 --> 08:33.303
Oh, don't worry.

08:33.887 --> 08:35.347
I come here often.

08:35.430 --> 08:37.766
Stay on dry ground
and it's perfectly safe.

08:38.892 --> 08:40.477
Uh, hmm.

08:41.186 --> 08:42.437
Hmm.

08:43.480 --> 08:44.606
Mm.

08:56.159 --> 08:57.327
Huh?

08:57.953 --> 08:59.246
Incredible.

08:59.955 --> 09:03.583
The inside of the dungeon
really is swarming with spirits, huh…

09:06.294 --> 09:09.464
I took some dirt and water from here
and added it to my jar.

09:10.924 --> 09:12.425
That explains it.

09:12.968 --> 09:15.095
So what do you come to this place to do?

09:15.178 --> 09:16.263
Hmm…

09:16.888 --> 09:19.599
I usually write letters
or do some reading.

09:20.225 --> 09:23.270
<i>Well, they weren't wrong</i>
<i>about her ditching class.</i>

09:26.439 --> 09:29.317
<i>Anyway, there's nothing dangerous yet.</i>

09:30.485 --> 09:31.736
<i>Wait.</i>

09:31.820 --> 09:35.323
<i>If we tilled this dirt</i>
<i>and planted some Mandrakes,</i>

09:35.407 --> 09:38.243
<i>I think we could safely utilize</i>
<i>the dungeon's mana.</i>

09:39.286 --> 09:43.081
<i>There's even a water source close by,</i>
<i>so it's definitely possible.</i>

09:44.916 --> 09:45.750
Huh?

09:47.043 --> 09:49.170
Oh, crap! This is bad!

09:49.254 --> 09:51.798
Just stand back!
I'll get rid of this Slime monster!

09:51.881 --> 09:53.592
Wait! No!

09:56.720 --> 09:58.471
What do you think you're doing?

10:00.599 --> 10:02.142
It won't come into the sunlight.

10:02.225 --> 10:03.977
You don't have to worry, I promise.

10:08.106 --> 10:10.525
Slimes are actually able
to break down bat droppings

10:10.609 --> 10:12.902
-and then turn them into mana.
-Oh.

10:13.987 --> 10:15.947
If the Slimes weren't here to do that,

10:16.031 --> 10:17.657
the dungeon would die.

10:20.368 --> 10:21.536
Bats, huh?

10:22.746 --> 10:24.164
-Take this.
-Huh?

10:36.468 --> 10:37.677
<i>It's good.</i>

10:38.511 --> 10:39.888
<i>If they're this good,</i>

10:39.971 --> 10:42.682
<i>I bet the animals around here</i>
<i>probably eat them.</i>

10:44.225 --> 10:47.270
<i>I wonder what kinds of things</i>
<i>the bats up there eat.</i>

10:48.355 --> 10:50.982
<i>And what season</i>
<i>do these raspberries grow in?</i>

10:51.066 --> 10:53.193
<i>What kind of animals eat them?</i>

10:54.402 --> 10:57.280
<i>I can't make a dungeon</i>
<i>without knowing things like that.</i>

11:02.077 --> 11:04.371
<i>I still have so much left to learn.</i>

11:09.042 --> 11:10.919
Thanks so much for bringing me here.

11:12.253 --> 11:13.380
The truth is,

11:13.463 --> 11:15.298
I thought if I just studied
spells and magic,

11:15.382 --> 11:16.925
that was all I need to know.

11:17.509 --> 11:18.802
But that's not true.

11:21.930 --> 11:24.683
Oh, I haven't introduced myself.

11:24.766 --> 11:26.309
My name's Falin.

11:26.393 --> 11:28.436
Would you mind telling me your name?

11:36.236 --> 11:37.737
My name is Marcille.

11:38.405 --> 11:41.658
Falin, what do you say
to becoming friends?

11:43.910 --> 11:45.995
The part about you
being the school's first genius

11:46.079 --> 11:47.580
has to be a lie, right?

11:47.664 --> 11:49.082
Why would you think it's a lie?

11:49.165 --> 11:51.710
I'll have you know
that I was an honor student!

11:53.294 --> 11:56.840
Anyway, this whole dungeon
is pretty unbelievable.

11:57.632 --> 11:59.926
There are layers
of calculations going on,

12:00.009 --> 12:02.303
and tons of mana being circulated.

12:02.971 --> 12:05.765
If the mad mage is really
out there somewhere,

12:05.849 --> 12:08.226
they're not just your average magic user.

12:09.436 --> 12:12.856
With that said, it's probably best
if you stopped living here, Senshi.

12:13.523 --> 12:14.983
Mind your own business.

12:15.567 --> 12:17.736
Seriously, you hate magic, right?

12:17.819 --> 12:20.447
While the dungeon itself
is entirely made out of it!

12:21.489 --> 12:22.699
Can't hear ya.

12:24.367 --> 12:25.702
I see.

12:25.785 --> 12:27.996
So Falin was talking about you.

12:29.038 --> 12:32.917
When she enrolled into magic school,
she would send me update letters,

12:33.001 --> 12:35.754
I could tell that
she was anxious there at first, but…

12:36.379 --> 12:39.382
<i>one day, she wrote about</i>
<i>how she made a new friend,</i>

12:39.466 --> 12:41.384
<i>and she sounded a lot happier.</i>

12:42.093 --> 12:43.470
Huh.

12:43.553 --> 12:46.264
She always praised you, Marcille.

12:47.307 --> 12:48.767
She thought you were awesome.

12:48.850 --> 12:49.976
Huh?

12:50.560 --> 12:51.603
Hm.

12:54.606 --> 12:56.524
Falin praised you too, Laios.

12:56.608 --> 12:58.109
She really looked up to you.

12:59.152 --> 13:00.904
Hm, is that so?

13:02.906 --> 13:04.115
What's so great about him?

13:04.199 --> 13:06.993
He's got the best dog impression
I've ever heard.

13:08.036 --> 13:12.123
<i>Maybe that's something I should</i>
<i>keep between me and Falin for now.</i>

13:12.207 --> 13:13.166
Well…

13:13.249 --> 13:16.127
let's get our butts in gear
and go save Falin!

13:17.670 --> 13:19.297
Come on, you tin can!

13:19.380 --> 13:21.800
You're awake,
so get up so we can get going!

13:23.885 --> 13:25.386
We're currently here.

13:25.970 --> 13:29.641
The orcs we talked to mentioned
the Red Dragon had appeared right here.

13:29.724 --> 13:31.392
It'll take two days to get there.

13:32.060 --> 13:34.354
It's probably not where we left it,

13:34.437 --> 13:37.315
but dragons also aren't really
the type to wander far.

13:38.066 --> 13:40.026
We should only make camp two more times.

13:40.693 --> 13:42.403
First, at the halfway mark,

13:42.487 --> 13:44.906
and lastly, right before the dragon.

13:44.989 --> 13:47.575
We'll wake up Laios
when the candle burns out.

13:48.243 --> 13:49.994
Do what you need now.

13:50.078 --> 13:51.704
We won't rest again for a while.

13:54.582 --> 13:56.084
I'd like to wash up.

13:57.460 --> 13:58.711
Seriously?

13:58.795 --> 14:00.338
I can do it in the corner.

14:01.798 --> 14:03.341
Just be quick about it.

14:07.595 --> 14:09.305
We'll be outside if you need us.

14:09.389 --> 14:11.975
Huh? Oh, it's fine if you stay.

14:12.058 --> 14:13.601
I'm not getting naked.

14:14.477 --> 14:15.979
Uh, okay.

14:17.897 --> 14:20.608
<i>Man, I sure do make them worry.</i>

14:21.568 --> 14:24.529
<i>Wonder if I should've studied</i>
<i>illusion magic too.</i>

14:25.363 --> 14:27.615
<i>No, that's not the problem.</i>

14:27.699 --> 14:30.118
<i>It's 'cause I'm the only girl</i>
<i>in the party now.</i>

14:31.536 --> 14:33.454
<i>We'll be parting ways here.</i>

14:34.080 --> 14:36.916
Are you serious?
Does it really have to be now?

14:37.000 --> 14:40.169
I mean, we still don't know
where Falin is after all.

14:41.754 --> 14:45.174
Sorry, but we have
our own livelihoods to worry about.

14:46.843 --> 14:49.596
<i>Just remembering that moment</i>
<i>makes me mad.</i>

14:50.138 --> 14:51.681
<i>I thought that we were all friends!</i>

14:56.644 --> 14:58.104
Wake up, Laios!

14:58.187 --> 14:59.689
Hey, come on!

14:59.772 --> 15:01.232
Time to get moving.

15:02.942 --> 15:04.736
There we go. Uh…

15:04.819 --> 15:06.905
Huh. Guess I boiled too much.

15:35.850 --> 15:37.310
An Undine!

15:41.230 --> 15:42.649
-Huh?
-What's wrong?

15:46.152 --> 15:47.612
What?

15:54.786 --> 15:56.245
My Water-Walking…

15:56.329 --> 15:57.622
The water is moving.

15:58.206 --> 16:00.333
Weapons won't work! We need fire!

16:00.959 --> 16:01.876
Fire?

16:03.711 --> 16:05.088
I'll start one.

16:05.171 --> 16:07.882
Hey, Marcille, hold on a bit longer!

16:07.966 --> 16:09.759
Easy for you to say.

16:11.135 --> 16:12.637
Please let this hit it.

16:23.398 --> 16:24.399
Uh?

16:32.740 --> 16:35.451
Marcille, what are you waiting for? Go!

16:35.994 --> 16:37.787
All of you, stay there!

16:37.870 --> 16:39.914
My Water-Walking spell is wearing off!

16:47.505 --> 16:48.673
Marcille!

16:48.756 --> 16:50.675
Get up! Keep moving!

16:59.642 --> 17:01.686
<i>I won't be able to run now.</i>

17:09.652 --> 17:11.112
<i>Where is it hiding?</i>

17:21.873 --> 17:24.917
I can't watch! Come on, Senshi, hurry up!

17:25.001 --> 17:26.711
I'm going as fast as I can!

17:26.794 --> 17:28.463
<i>This is bad.</i>

17:28.546 --> 17:29.589
Huh?

17:31.507 --> 17:33.760
<i>I don't have much mana left.</i>

17:33.843 --> 17:35.928
<i>I've got to get it in the next shot.</i>

17:41.809 --> 17:42.685
<i>Where?</i>

17:43.936 --> 17:45.104
<i>Where is it?</i>

17:45.938 --> 17:47.982
<i>There must be some kind of clue.</i>

17:49.275 --> 17:50.151
<i>There!</i>

17:51.527 --> 17:53.154
<i>It has my blood.</i>

17:53.946 --> 17:55.406
It's so fast.

17:55.490 --> 17:56.824
Hmm.

18:02.830 --> 18:05.249
Just hold on!

18:08.836 --> 18:12.256
Got--

18:21.808 --> 18:23.518
-Hey, guys?
-Uh?

18:24.560 --> 18:25.686
What now?

18:28.606 --> 18:30.316
All right, here's the plan.

18:33.528 --> 18:35.822
Let's get out of here!

18:41.786 --> 18:43.621
How are you holding up, Marcille?

18:43.704 --> 18:45.957
I stopped the bleeding,

18:46.040 --> 18:48.126
but I'm low on blood and mana.

18:49.043 --> 18:50.419
So I'm spent.

18:51.254 --> 18:52.463
Sorry.

18:52.547 --> 18:53.422
It's fine.

18:53.506 --> 18:54.966
Just take it easy.

18:55.925 --> 18:57.176
Mm.

18:57.260 --> 19:01.347
I really should've paid more attention
when Falin was teaching me healing magic.

19:02.265 --> 19:04.559
-Hey, Laios?
-Huh?

19:05.268 --> 19:07.061
What are we gonna do now?

19:07.145 --> 19:11.107
There's no way we can take a mana-less
magic user further into the dungeon.

19:11.190 --> 19:12.608
And we can't continue on

19:12.692 --> 19:14.861
without the help
of her Water-Walking spell.

19:14.944 --> 19:17.196
Let's wait
for other adventurers to pass by.

19:17.989 --> 19:20.199
If we're lucky,
one of them will be a healer.

19:20.783 --> 19:22.994
There's no way
that someone who's willing to help others

19:23.077 --> 19:25.246
would conveniently pass by here.

19:25.329 --> 19:27.582
Besides, we don't have anything
we can trade.

19:28.166 --> 19:30.877
Yeah, I think the only thing we have
is Kelpie meat.

19:30.960 --> 19:33.087
Let's hope the person is starving.

19:33.171 --> 19:36.299
It's a rare nutrient source in a dungeon.

19:36.382 --> 19:39.635
Who cares about nutrition right now?

19:39.719 --> 19:41.596
Actually…

19:41.679 --> 19:44.640
did you happen to grab
its liver too, Senshi?

19:44.724 --> 19:45.975
Of course I did.

19:46.058 --> 19:48.686
Livers are too rich in iron
to leave behind.

19:49.228 --> 19:50.146
Hm?

19:50.688 --> 19:51.606
Huh?

19:51.689 --> 19:52.982
I knew it.

19:53.733 --> 19:54.984
That means…

19:56.444 --> 19:58.446
-It's grilling time!
-It's grilling time!

20:05.036 --> 20:08.497
Mane, neck, liver,

20:08.581 --> 20:13.502
ribs, tail, thigh, loin,

20:13.586 --> 20:15.129
and veggies.

20:15.213 --> 20:19.133
KELPIE GRILLED MEAT

20:20.009 --> 20:20.885
Marcille.

20:20.968 --> 20:22.762
-Mm?
-Marcille.

20:24.805 --> 20:26.140
Are you good to sit up?

20:26.224 --> 20:28.893
We made something nice for you.

20:45.368 --> 20:46.285
Thigh.

20:47.036 --> 20:48.287
Where's the liver?

20:48.371 --> 20:51.457
You got to make sure
organs get cooked all the way.

20:55.169 --> 20:58.047
Forgive me, Marcille. But I'm digging in.

21:00.383 --> 21:01.634
Mm.

21:01.717 --> 21:03.052
It's pretty good.

21:03.135 --> 21:06.055
Yeah, it's a little chewy, but I like it.

21:06.138 --> 21:09.850
Does it taste more like a horse
or a marine animal?

21:10.518 --> 21:13.562
I haven't eaten either,
so I can't really compare it.

21:14.272 --> 21:15.189
Ribs.

21:15.982 --> 21:17.733
It tastes sweet, doesn't it?

21:17.817 --> 21:19.568
Yeah, it's so soft.

21:19.652 --> 21:21.612
Marcille, the liver is ready now.

21:22.822 --> 21:23.739
Tenderloin.

21:24.699 --> 21:26.993
Oh, it feels like
it's melting in my mouth.

21:27.076 --> 21:28.369
I really like this one.

21:29.036 --> 21:30.579
Here's some liver, Marcille.

21:31.330 --> 21:32.373
Tail.

21:33.082 --> 21:34.083
Yummy.

21:34.166 --> 21:36.877
An interesting flavor on this one.

21:36.961 --> 21:38.212
Here, Marcille.

21:38.879 --> 21:40.965
Have more liver, Marcille.

21:41.048 --> 21:42.591
How is it, Marcille?

21:42.675 --> 21:44.218
Eat some more, Marcille.

21:44.302 --> 21:45.886
You like it, Marcille?

21:50.975 --> 21:52.059
Please…

21:52.768 --> 21:53.728
Huh?

21:53.811 --> 21:56.981
Please give me the other parts, too!

21:58.774 --> 22:00.484
-Uh…
-Oh.

22:01.152 --> 22:03.321
Well, it looks like
she's starting to recover.

22:03.404 --> 22:04.989
Liver is amazing.

22:05.698 --> 22:08.492
That aside,
what do we do about her low mana?

22:08.576 --> 22:11.495
Yeah, if only there was a meat
that could help restore it.

22:11.579 --> 22:14.248
Why did you stuff the Basilisk
with mana herbs?

22:14.332 --> 22:16.125
I still stand by my choice.

22:21.964 --> 22:23.466
Do you smell that?

22:24.300 --> 22:25.885
It's coming from below.

22:25.968 --> 22:27.553
What is that?

22:27.636 --> 22:29.889
I think it's grilled meat.

22:30.473 --> 22:32.350
Someone below must be cooking it.

22:33.142 --> 22:35.686
Jeez.

22:35.770 --> 22:37.772
You got to be kidding me.

22:38.481 --> 22:41.025
What kind of moron
would be grilling meat in here?
